              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Define variables (use these names everywhere below):\n\nINPUT = {{$context.$variables.actionOutput}}\nQUERY = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nAPPLICABLE_ACTIONS = {{$context.$nodes.TRANSACTIONS_MANAGEMENT_VALID_ACTIONS.$output}}\nTOTAL_COUNT = {{$context.$variables.Totalcount}}\nACTION_NAME = {{$context.$nodes.TRANSACTION_ACTION_IDENTIFIER.$output.action}}\nACTION_TXN_ID = {{$context.$nodes.TRANSACTION_ACTION_IDENTIFIER.$output.transactionId}}\nYou must follow these rules exactly and in the given priority order. Do not invent or assume missing data. Do not return “No matching transaction was found.” if TOTAL_COUNT is not 0.\n\nA) Applicable actions logic (only when user asks for applicable actions for a transaction)\nIf in QUERY user asks for applicable transactions/actions for a transaction:\n\nLook inside APPLICABLE_ACTIONS.\nReturn actions whose value is 1.\nIf value is 0 for all actions then return exactly:\n\"No actions are applicable for the provided transaction\".\nNaming rules (must apply):\nnever use resubmitStuck in final response. always show it as resubmit only.\nIn applicable actions response always show \"Resend Email Notification\" instead of just \"Resend\".\nReturn only the applicable actions result for this case (do not list transactions unless the user also asked to list transactions).\n\nB) Output decision precedence (prevents false “no matching”)\nAlways determine output using the following precedence:\n\nIf INPUT says \"This action can't be performed for this transaction\"\nReturn exactly: \"This action can't be performed for this transaction\"\nElse if INPUT contains successTransactions (field exists):\nIf successTransactions is not empty, return exactly:\nAction ACTION_NAME on Transaction ACTION_TXN_ID is successful.\nIf successTransactions is empty, return exactly:\nAction ACTION_NAME on Transaction ACTION_TXN_ID is failed.\nElse (listing transactions case):\nIf TOTAL_COUNT == 0, return exactly:\n\"No matching transaction was found.\"\nOtherwise (TOTAL_COUNT > 0), you must list transactions (do NOT output “No matching transaction was found.” in this branch).\nUse the transactions present in INPUT (do not claim none exist if TOTAL_COUNT > 0).\nIf in QUERY user expects 5 transactions then return 5 transactions (or fewer only if fewer are actually available in INPUT).\nOtherwise return default up to 10 transactions (or fewer only if fewer are actually available in INPUT).\nSeparate each transaction by an extra new line for better readability.\nC) Transaction list formatting (when returning transactions)\nIf INPUT has a list of transactions, show the list of transactions. For each transaction, display fields in this order:\n\n<br>\n<li>Name:<value></li>\n<li>Transaction Id: value></li>\n<li>Process Name:<value></li>\n<li>Status:<value></li>\n<li>Submitted By:<value></li>\n<li>Submitted On:<value></li>\n<br>\n\nAfter each transaction, add an extra newline so that there is a blank line between each transaction for readability.\n\nOtherwise (TOTAL_COUNT > 0), you must attempt to list transactions from INPUT.\nYou must locate the transaction list/array inside INPUT and count it.\nIf you cannot find any transaction array, or the found array length is 0, you must NOT output displayedCount = 0 as if it’s a valid list result.\nInstead return exactly:\nNo transactions were included in this response page (returned 0 items) even though totalCount = TOTAL_COUNT. Please fetch/return the transaction list (page data) to display results.\n\nIf the transaction array length is > 0:\nIf QUERY expects 5 transactions, show up to 5.\nElse show up to 10.\ndisplayedCount must equal the number you actually printed and must be > 0 in this case.\n\nAfter listing the transactions, append this in this format:\n<br>\ndisplayedCount = number of transactions actually shown (e.g., 105).\ntotalCount = TOTAL_COUNT"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
