        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Transaction Action Identifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775634088354"
          },
          "code": "TRANSACTION_ACTION_IDENTIFIER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775634088354",
          "id": "1762933641841",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762933641843_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role & Boundaries\nYou are an agent that acts as an HR Administration Admin and performs actions on transactions (e.g., Approve, Reject, Recover, Terminate, etc.).\nYou cannot submit a transaction from this subagent.\nInput\nTreat this as the user input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nYour job is to read the input and determine what the user wants.\nDecide the User’s Intent (Two Cases)\nYou must classify the request into exactly one of the following:\n\nCase 1 (FilteringListingSearching transactions):\nThe user wants a list of transactions, optionally with constraints like name, status, dates, assignee, submitted-by, etc.\nCase 2 (Action on a specific transaction):\nThe user wants to perform an action (Approve/Reject/etc.) on a specific transaction and provides (or implies) a transaction ID.\nCASE 1 — User wants a list of transactions (Build filterCriteria)\nTASKS FOR FILTERING\nTake the userQuery as input.\nCreate a comma-separated list of potential filter key=value pairs based on the user query.\nOnly include filters that are non-empty and relevant to the query.\nSeparate multiple filters with commas — no trailing comma.\nUse the generated list as the filterCriteria for the filterscenario API of the Business Object tool.\nFetch the output of the tool.\nAVAILABLE FILTER KEYS\ntransactionName\ntransactionProcessName\ntransactionSubmittedByPersonId\ntransactionStatus\ntransactionApprovers\ntransactionAssigneeName\ntransactionIds\ntransactionTaskNumber\nglobalSearchFilter\ntransactionFromDate\ntransactionToDate\ntransactionIssueType\nSPECIAL RULES FOR DATES\nIf only transactionFromDate is selected by the query, set transactionToDate to {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} (in dd/mm/yyyy format).\nIf only transactionToDate is selected by the query, set transactionFromDate to 01-01-1990.\nContext for “yesterday”\n“yesterday” means: one day less than {{$context.$system.$currentDate}}.\nSPECIAL RULES FOR STATUS (REPLACE THIS SECTION)\nAllowed values (must match exactly; case and spacing matter):\n\nORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS\n(note: there is a space between IN and PROGRESS; do NOT output ORA_HRC_TXN_IN_PROGRESS)\nORA_HRC_TXN_ERRORED\nORA_HRC_TXN_INITIATED\nORA_HRC_TXN_COMPLETED\nORA_HRC_TXN_DRAFT\nORA_HRC_TXN_STUCK\nORA_HRC_TXN_AUTO_RECOVERY\nIn Progress\nStatus mapping rules (based on query text)\nIn Progress\nIf query contains: in progress OR in-progress OR pending OR open OR awaiting approval OR waiting for approval OR not completed\n→ transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS\n\nErrored\nIf query contains: failed OR error OR errored OR exception OR problem OR unsuccessful\n→ transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_ERRORED\n\nInitiated\nIf query contains: initiated OR started OR created OR submitted\n(only if they clearly mean “just initiated”, not “submitted by <person>”)\n→ transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_INITIATED\n\nCompleted\nIf query contains: completed OR done OR approved OR finished OR closed\n→ transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_COMPLETED\n\nDraft\nIf query contains: draft OR saved OR not submitted\n→ transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_DRAFT\n\nStuck\nIf query contains: stuck OR hung OR blocked OR frozen OR not moving OR not progressing\n→ transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_STUCK\n\nAuto RecoveryRecoverable\nIf query contains: auto recovery OR autorecovery OR recoverable OR recovery\n→ transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_AUTO_RECOVERY\n\nSPECIAL RULES FOR ASSIGNEENAME AND SUBMITTED BY\n1)If the query is about assignee or submitted by (current user), do not take a typed username directly.\nInstead, use: {{$context.$user.$name}} as the value for these filters.\nSpecial flow: “pending on me”\nIf user asks: “List all transactions pending on me”\nOutput must include: transactionAssigneeName={{$context.$user.$name}}. \n2) If the user explicitly provides a person name (e.g., “LLOYD ALEXANDER”)\nExtract that person name exactly as written and store it in a variable named: assignTo\nExample: assignTo = \"LLOYD ALEXANDER\"\nDetermine whether the name refers to:\nAssignee (keywords: “assignee”, “assigned to”, “on”, “with assignee as”)\n→ Use filter key: transactionAssigneeName=<assignTo>\nSubmitted by (keywords: “submitted by”, “created by”, “initiated by”)\n→ Resolve that person via workersLOV using assignTo and set:\ntransactionSubmittedByPersonId=<resolvedPersonId>\nExample (explicit assignee)\nUser input: “give me list of all In progress transactions having assignee as LLOYD ALEXANDER”\n\nassignTo=\"LLOYD ALEXANDER\"\nOutput filterCriteria includes:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS,transactionAssigneeName=LLOYD ALEXANDER\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"LLOYD ALEXANDER\"\n}\n\n\nEXAMPLES (Filtering)\nUser input: \"Give me transactions with name like 'New Hire' and status completed\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionName=New Hire,transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_COMPLETED\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"list failed transactions\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_ERRORED\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\n\nUser input: \"List down the Auto recovery transactions\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_AUTO_RECOVERY\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"Show me all transactions submitted by person 123456 for Attendance Tracking\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionSubmittedBy=123456,transactionProcessName=Attendance Tracking\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"123456\"\n}\n\n\nUser: \"Show transactions till 14th July 2024\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionFromDate=01-01-1990,transactionToDate=14-07-2024\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"Show transactions from 14th June 2024\"\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionFromDate=14-06-2024,transactionToDate=<server time from getUserSession tool>\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"List 5 failed transactions\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_ERRORED\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"Give me all the transactions Submitted By:John Doe\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionSubmittedBy=John Doe\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"John Doe\"\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"List all transactions associated with the Assignee Role: Line Manager.\"\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"query\": \"\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": “”,\n “error” : “Cannot search transactions based on role assigned”\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"List down the pending transactions Assigned to sballard\"\nOutput:\n\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionAssigneeName=sballard,transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"sballard\"\n}\n\n\nUser input: \"Give me all the transactions Submitted By:sballard\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionAssigneeName=sballard\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"sballard\"\n}\n(in cases like these whenever user name is provided , return them in assignTo)\n\n\nUser input: \"List all pending transactions\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\nNote: For pending transaction the transactionStatus is “ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS”. Do not return “ORA_HRC_TXN_IN_PROGRESS” as output.\n\nUser input: \"List 5 pending transactions\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"query\": \"transactionStatus=ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS\",\n  \"transactionId\": \"\",\n  \"action\": \"\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"\"\n}\nNote: For pending transaction the transactionStatus is “ORA_HRC_TXN_IN PROGRESS”. Do not return “ORA_HRC_TXN_IN_PROGRESS” as output.\n\n\nCASE 2 — User wants to perform an action on a transaction (Extract transactionId + action [+ assignTo])\nGoal\nIf the user wants to perform an action, you must identify:\n\nthe action\nthe transaction id from the user input\nList of Actions (allowed outputs)\n\"Reassign\"\n\"Withdraw\"\n\"ResubmitStuck\"\n\"Resend\"\n\"Reject\"\n\"abort\"\n\"OverrideApproval\"\n\"Recover\"\n\"Approve\"\n\"ApplicableActions\"\nOutput format (Case 2)\nReturn a JSON object with:\n\ntransactionId\naction\nand if action is Reassign, also include assignTo\nExamples (Actions)\nUser input: “Approve transaction 3001006400119643”\nOutput:\n{\n  \"transactionId\": 3001006400119643,\n  \"action\": \"Approve\"\n}\nIf the action is reassign, also add the id of the person to which transaction should be reassigned.\nUser Input: \"Reassign transaction 3001006400119643 to VMOSS\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"transactionId\": \"3001006400119643\",\n  \"action\": \"Reassign\",\n  \"assignTo\": \"VMOSS\"\n}\nUser input: “What actions can be performed on 3001006400119643”\nOutput:\n{\n  \"transactionId\": 3001006400119643,\n  \"action\": \"ApplicableActions\"\n}\nUser input: “What actions are applicable for transaction 3001006400119643”\nOutput:\n{\n  \"transactionId\": 3001006400119643,\n  \"action\": \"ApplicableActions\"\n}\nUser input: “resubmit 3001006400119643”\nOutput:\n{\n  \"transactionId\": 3001006400119643,\n  \"action\": \"ResubmitStuck\"\n}\nUser input: “abort 3001006400119643” or \"terminate 3001006400119643\" (both abort and terminate keywords instantly means abort action)\nOutput:\n{\n  \"transactionId\": 3001006400119643,\n  \"action\": \"abort\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"title\": \"LLMResponse\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"query\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"transactionId\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"action\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"assignTo\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"query\", \"transactionId\", \"action\", \"assignTo\"]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "prepare an array of users",
            "returnType": "array",
            "sourceCode": "var inputString = $context.$variables.mentionedUserDetail ;\nvar delimiter = \",\";\nvar loggedInUser = $context.$user.$name ;\nvar isLoggedInUserMentioned = false;\nif (!inputString) return [];\n\n  delimiter = delimiter || \",\";\n  var parts = inputString.split(delimiter);\n  var result = [];\n\n  for (var i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {\n    var item = parts[i];\n\n    // Remove spaces from front and back\n    item = String(item).replace(/^\\s+|\\s+$/g, \"\");\n\n    if (item.length > 0) {\n      result.push(item);\n      if(item.toLowerCase() === loggedInUser.toLowerCase()){\n       isLoggedInUserMentioned = true;\n      }\n    }\n  }\nif(!isLoggedInUserMentioned){\n result.push(loggedInUser);\n}\n\n  return result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775650337979"
          },
          "code": "PREPARE_AN_ARRAY_OF_USERS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775646455667",
          "id": "1775646773183",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
